# Cloudflare Pages SPA rewrite.
#
# The web export is a single page app (app.json `web.output: "single"`), so every deep
# route has to be served the same index.html and resolved client-side by expo-router.
#
# The `200` status is the entire point of moving off GitHub Pages. Pages has no rewrite
# support, so the only way to serve an SPA there is to copy index.html to 404.html, which
# means every deep route answers with an HTTP 404 while rendering correctly. That is
# invisible in a browser but not to a crawler, and both app stores FETCH the privacy
# policy URL they are given. Here the rewrite serves the app with a real 200.
#
# Ordering matters: _redirects is evaluated top to bottom, and Cloudflare serves any
# genuine static file (assets under _expo/, favicon.ico, privacy/index.html) before
# consulting this rule, so the catch-all cannot shadow real files.
/*    /index.html   200
